This project reimplements, in TypeScript, the decision-loop design of
jev-ultrafast by Browser Use:

  https://github.com/browser-use/jev-ultrafast  (MIT License)

That project is Python and drives a local Chrome over raw CDP. This one is an
independent implementation. It keeps the core idea -- ask a classifier to pick
one operation and one target from an indexed table of the page's controls, and
call a small language model only to write field text -- and adds support for
open shadow DOM, same-origin and cross-origin iframes, nested scrolling, file
uploads, pop-up tabs, native selects, keyboard-only widgets, and canvas
reporting. No code was copied.

The classifier is TypeSafe's Jev: https://docs.typesafe.ai
